    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33920" root="فشح" body-key="f">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَشَحَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَشَحَ</span></b> , (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَشْحٌ</span>, (TK,) <i>He</i> (a
man, TK) <i>parted his legs,</i> or <i>made an opening
between them;</i> (K;) like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَشَجَ</span>; both mentioned
by Th, on the authority of IAar; (TA;) as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فشّح</span></b> , (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفْشِيحٌ</span>; and likewise with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ج</span>,
as mentioned by Th. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَشَحَ عَنْهُ</span>,
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فشّح</span></b> , <i>He declined, deviated,</i> or <i>turned aside</i>
or <i>away, from him,</i> or <i>it;</i> (K;) and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَشَجَ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فشّج</span>. (TA.)

